# core v3.7 — NEGATIVE. An attachment with no algorithm. Violation constraint
# 3 of 3, and the least obvious of the three.
#
# The path is there and the digest is there, so a reader might call this
# complete. It is not, and the shapes file states why in one line: without the
# algorithm the digest cannot be RECOMPUTED, and a digest that cannot be
# recomputed cannot be checked, which makes the previous requirement decorative.
# The node would then assert integrity it does not provide.
#
# The digest length does not rescue it. cascade:contentHash is constrained to
# lowercase hex of at least 32 characters and NOT to a fixed length, precisely
# so the algorithm can be replaced; a 64-character value is consistent with
# SHA-256 and also with several other functions, so guessing from the length is
# not a check, it is an assumption. Nor does the path: the `{algorithm}` segment
# is a producer's filing choice, and RFC 6920 registry tokens are what
# cascade:hashAlgorithm is for.
#
# Rejected by cascade:AttachmentShape / cascade:hashAlgorithm / sh:minCount 1.
#
# Fully synthetic.

@prefix cascade: <https://ns.cascadeprotocol.org/core/v1#> .

<urn:uuid:a77a0307-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a4> a cascade:Attachment ;
    cascade:attachmentPath
        "attachments/sha-256/8dd3c6b5f593b25cb9dc0094d67323d16c3bbc9584eda019726a38dd2cc7a471" ;
    cascade:contentHash
        "8dd3c6b5f593b25cb9dc0094d67323d16c3bbc9584eda019726a38dd2cc7a471" ;
    cascade:attachmentMediaType "application/pdf" ;
    cascade:attachmentTitle "Comprehensive Metabolic Panel — signed report" .
